### HTML Escaping

```typescript
function escapeHtml(text: string): string {
  return text
    .replace(/&/g, '&amp;')
    .replace(/</g, '&lt;')
    .replace(/>/g, '&gt;')
    .replace(/"/g, '&quot;')
    .replace(/'/g, '&#039;');
}
```

Apply to all user-controlled content:
- summary.title, summary.impact, summary.keyPoints, summary.action
- metadata.from (email addresses can contain special chars)

